    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "e44170f23f4dca2b86823c3dfb6fbc1f33c96fb3",
      "message": "Enemy conditional-effect class \u2014 three presentation repairs (coating consequence, Resonance Cascade, enemy control)\n\nOwner ruling accepted the enemy conditional-effect class audit in full and\ndirected exactly three bounded presentation repairs. No mechanic in this\nclass was changed \u2014 Venomous's -2 attack-roll penalty stands as designed,\nand every number below already existed in production before this commit.\n\nRepair 1 \u2014 enemy weapon coating explains its lingering consequence.\nenemyCoating.ts gains `ailmentConsequenceLabel(kind)`, stating each already-\napplied ailment's real number (poisoned -2 attack, armor_severed -2 AC,\nchilled -2 DEX, burn_scar +50% aetheric damage taken) as one canonical\nphrase. combatResolution.ts's coating hit line and EnemyPanel.tsx's two\ncapability-description surfaces (enemyDetailBody + the expanded popup JSX)\nall now state it. Corruption says it raises the corruption meter; electrical\nsays nothing extra, since it has no lingering effect. No coating spawn rate,\ndamage, duration, or proc behavior changed.\n\nRepair 2 \u2014 Resonance Cascade explains itself. aetherTechniques.ts's\ndescribeTechniqueTrait() special-cases `technique:resonance_cascade` to\nstate the real tactical facts already in combatResolution.ts's\nenemyChannelsTechnique (cornered below 35% HP, 5d10 direct damage halved by\naetheric resistance, 1d10 kickback to the enemy, once per combat) without\nexposing internal implementation terms. The other three technique traits\n(aether_shield/temporal_slip/veil_of_ether) are self-buffs outside this\nclass and keep their bare \"Channels: X\" form.\n\nRepair 3 \u2014 enemy control state reaches the panel. EnemyView gains an\noptional `control` field threaded from `currentScene.enemyControl[idx]`\n(ExplorationScreen.tsx) \u2014 the one existing typed authority in\nenemyControl.ts. EnemyDetailContent's ACTIVE EFFECTS section now renders a\ncurrently-controlled enemy's state (skip kinds: \"skips its turn\"; hinder\nkinds: the real controlAttackPenalty number) beside the coating DOTs, using\nthe same plain accent-dot treatment already used for non-coating statuses \u2014\nnever as a trait/capability chip, and never fabricating a duration control\ndoesn't have. Brace/internal state (enemyBraced) is untouched and not\nsurfaced. Control mechanics, duration, application, and combat resolution\nare unchanged.\n\nTests: extended ota1656TheBladeYouCanSee.test.ts (Repair 1) and\nota1202EnemyTechniques.test.ts (Repair 2), added\nenemyConditionalEffectControlSurfacing.test.tsx (Repair 3, 9 cases). 79\ndirectly-affected tests pass (including the pre-existing QOL #220 suite,\nconfirming no regression to the accepted coating/effects geometry), plus a\ntargeted 149-test batch across combat/control/coating suites. Typecheck and\nlint clean. aerial/aetherkin trait-chip fallback (noted by the audit) is\nout of scope, left as recorded follow-up. HAL untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
